title: Genesis 15 – Abram Believed God
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 15: the word of the LORD came to Abram, he believed and it was counted to him for righteousness, the covenant of the pieces, and the reprobate doctrine.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-15-abram-believed-god.html

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 15 study
# (posts 6879-6886, 6898, 6899). Fixed: "they mercy" -> "the mercy"; "Reparation" -> "Reprobation";
# "testimony necessitates" -> "testament necessitates" (Hebrews 9:16-17); "of they can" -> "if they can".

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 15 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 15: Abram Believed God
sub: Counted for Righteousness • The Seed • The Covenant
refs: Genesis 15:1-21
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The word of the Lord
--- Fear Not, Abram
kicker: v. 1
sub: The Word of the {Lord} Came unto Abram in a Vision
scripture: Genesis 15:1 | mark: Fear not, Abram: I am thy shield, and thy exceeding great reward
p: The word of God came to Abram in a vision. The Bible tells us who the word of God is. It is Jesus. [[John 1:1-2]]

--- {Lord} God, What Wilt Thou Give Me?
kicker: vv. 2–5
sub: So Shall Thy Seed Be
scripture: Genesis 15:2-5 | mark: he that shall come forth out of thine own bowels shall be thine heir; So shall thy seed be
p: Abram, old when he called upon the name of the {Lord} and received blessings and promises, now even older and without a true heir, questions the {Lord}. Abram’s faith tested, the word of God brings him forth to tell the stars.

--- He Believed in the {Lord}
kicker: v. 6
sub: And He Counted It to Him for Righteousness
scripture: Genesis 15:6 | mark: he believed in the LORD; and he counted it to him for righteousness
p: This is the promise made when *he believed in the {Lord}; and he counted it to him for righteousness*. That his righteousness was imputed for that faith, by a gracious God. And it was faith in that seed to be given by the {Lord}, and the blessings for that heir and the promise made in Him.

--- Counted for Righteousness
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 15:6
fig: Romans 4:3-5 | Romans 4:3-5
fig: James 2:23 | James 2:23 | [[lesson:post-abraham-justified-by-faith-james-2|Abraham saved by faith alone, and James 2]]

--- The Children of Abraham
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 15:5–6
fig: Galatians 3:6-9 | Galatians 3:6-9
fig: Galatians 3:16 | Galatians 3:16

--- Heirs According to the Promise
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 15:5
fig: Galatians 3:29 | Galatians 3:29
fig: Revelation 7:9-10 | Revelation 7:9-10 | In Him the promise of a nation innumerable, like the stars in the sky, is fulfilled in Revelation 7.

--- So Shall Thy Seed Be
kicker: Application • Genesis 15:5
sub: Not for the Modern Jew, but of Christ and Him Crucified
p: We see in scripture that this promise was kept, his seed being one, Jesus Christ. Following the tribulation and the rapture, there are saints redeemed in the blood of Christ: 144,000 Old Testament saints, 12,000 from each of the tribes listed (not Jews, but Israelites), and *a great multitude, which no man could number, of all nations, and kindreds, and people, and tongues*. [[1 Thessalonians 4:16-17]]
callout: This is the promise to Abraham. Not for the modern Jew. Not for the apostate and wicked modern state calling itself Israel. But of Christ and Him crucified, with the power to make the elect heirs to the Kingdom of Heaven: whosoever will call upon the name of the {Lord}. Old Testament. New Testament. The same dispensation. The same promise. The same faith.

--- God Doesn’t Break His Promises
kicker: Application • Genesis 15:5
sub: Not Knowing Scripture They Err
p: Dispensationalist Christians who say “God doesn’t break His promises!” don’t understand what the promises are, and don’t believe they are fulfilled in Christ. They cannot rightly divide the word of God, for whatever reason, and they allow wicked men with a Satanic agenda to tell them what it all means. And so, they twist themselves into knots trying to square the wicked doctrines of different paths to righteousness, one of works, one of blood, one of faith; the wicked doctrine of pre-trib rapture; the invention that the millennial Kingdom is for the modern Jew. Not knowing scripture they err, and do not understand what they affirm. [[1 Timothy 1:7]]

=== The covenant
--- Whereby Shall I Know?
kicker: vv. 7–11
sub: An Heifer, a She Goat, a Ram, a Turtledove and a Pigeon
scripture: Genesis 15:7-11 | mark: whereby shall I know that I shall inherit it
p: Each a sign or a picture of Christ. As established in the Levitical laws, 400 and more years from when this is happening, done to show the mercy of God in redemption by faith: the blood offerings, the sin offerings, the burnt offerings. A testament necessitates a blood offering. These were a symbol of Christ’s. [[Hebrews 9:16-18]]

--- A Horror of Great Darkness
kicker: vv. 12–14
sub: Thy Seed Shall Be a Stranger in a Land That Is Not Theirs
scripture: Genesis 15:12-14 | mark: thy seed shall be a stranger in a land that is not theirs; four hundred years
p: In a deep sleep, a darkness fell upon Abram, and the word of God prophesied the time to come: the sojourning in Egypt and enslavement. Moses writing in the Spirit of the prophecy of Exodus given to Abraham.

--- The Iniquity of the Amorites
kicker: vv. 15–16
sub: Is Not Yet Full
scripture: Genesis 15:15-16 | mark: the iniquity of the Amorites is not yet full
p: The {Lord} telling Abram that he himself will die knowing peace, but that the land will not be given unto his descendants until the wickedness of the Amorites comes in. They are going to purge the land of Canaan of the wicked, as an instrument of the {Lord}.

--- A Burning Lamp
kicker: vv. 17–21
sub: From the River of Egypt unto the Great River
scripture: Genesis 15:17-21 | mark: a smoking furnace, and a burning lamp that passed between those pieces; from the river of Egypt unto the great river, the river Euphrates
p: A furnace and a lamp appeared on the offerings, passing between those pieces laid on an altar: a testament signed by God. The Jews, so-called, will today say they rightly own “Greater Israel,” from the river to the sea, citing this verse. Basically from the Red Sea to the Euphrates, including Syria, parts of Jordan, Saudi Arabia, and Iraq. They claim it is their birthright, and believe if they can secure these lands by whatever means necessary, they will be given a kingdom on earth. But that’s not for them.

--- The Holy City
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 15:18
fig: Revelation 21:3 | Revelation 21:3
fig: Revelation 21:27 | Revelation 21:27
refs: Revelation 21:1-2; Revelation 21:22-26

=== The reprobate doctrine
--- The Reprobate Doctrine
kicker: A doctrine worth knowing • Genesis 15:16
sub: One of the Most Overlooked but Relevant Doctrines in the Bible
p: One of the most important doctrines, which touches on both the spiritual nature of man and a warning to heed here on earth, is the reprobate doctrine. It is taught throughout both Old and New Testament, which not only gives description of how one becomes a reprobate, but example after example of those that do, and warning after warning of how to handle them. Reprobation, the final and utter rejection by God of those who have finally and utterly rejected His overtures of grace, the call to Christ and the prodding and patience of the Holy Ghost, is one of the three spiritual states of man. [[Romans 1:28]]

--- The Three Spiritual States of Man
kicker: A doctrine worth knowing • Genesis 15:16
table: State | Who they are
tr: **The unregenerate sinner** | Dead in spirit but with the conscience of God within, who, until death, could hear the call and believe on Jesus Christ and be saved. The children of disobedience. [[Ephesians 2:2]]
tr: **The saved** | Those who call upon the name of the {Lord}, believing God’s testimony, spirit quickened. Born again believers. Called the sons of God. [[John 1:12]]
tr: **The reprobate** | Twice dead. Conscience seared. Hearts hardened, ears dulled. Unable to come to the knowledge of the truth. Rejected of God. Given up. Clouds without water. The children of the devil. [[Jude 1:12]]

--- Lumped In with the Common Sinner
kicker: A doctrine worth knowing • Genesis 15:16
sub: An Inability to Understand Evil
p: Often Christians, seeking to be kind and show mercy, thinking they are doing the right thing, will completely ignore the final group, lumping them in with the common sinner. Holding out hope, even when they reveal their wickedness in ways exactly as God’s word tells us they will. Evil often isn’t an outward appearance of malevolence like a comic book super villain. It’s often someone who is a miserable human being. We take pity on them, and they use our good-natured inclination for mercy and grace to take advantage of us. They are the false teachers, the false prophets bringing doctrines of damnation, whited sepulchres. [[Matthew 23:27-33]]
callout: I encourage all of you to study the reprobate doctrine and come to an understanding, to better defend yourself, your family and your community from these people. [[lesson:topic-reprobate|The Reprobate Mind]]

--- The Same Promise, the Same Faith
center: Abram believed in the {Lord}, and He counted it to him for righteousness. The promise was kept in his seed, which is Christ, and through Him Abraham has heirs too numerous to count, whosoever will call upon the name of the {Lord}.
